.SH EXAMPLES
One DVB\-T multiplex on a HackRF, a test pattern and a film:
.PP
.RS
.EX
[network]
name = "Ma TV"
provider = "Ma TV"

[[radio]]
name = "hackrf"
driver = "hackrf"
gain = 30

[[carrier]]
name = "Mux 1"
radio = "hackrf"
channel = 22                       # 482 MHz, DVB\-T 8k 64\-QAM 7/8 1/32
  [[carrier.service]]
  name = "Mire"
  source = "lavfi:testsrc2=size=1280x720:rate=25"
  encode = { video_bitrate = "3M" }
  [[carrier.service]]
  name = "Film"
  source = "/srv/videos/film.mkv"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Two adjacent multiplexes on one radio (LO 486 MHz, 18.29 MS/s), live sources with a guide:
.PP
.RS
.EX
[network]
name = "BsT"
onid = 0x20FA
network_id = 0x20FA

[epg]
dir = "/var/lib/dvbtx/epg"

[defaults]
backup = "/var/lib/dvbtx/backup.ts"

[[radio]]
name = "hackrf"
driver = "hackrf"

[[carrier]]
name = "Mux 1"
radio = "hackrf"
frequency = 482_000_000
  [[carrier.service]]
